//
// olmo2_1b_q4nx prefill TTFT vs prompt length, into olmo2_1b_q4nx.prefill_sweep.json
// (collected by the nightly LLM benchmark). It times the fused prefill that
// run, verify and profile use: chunked, any prompt up to the length it was
// built for, so sweep_prefill.py --fused builds it once for the longest length
// and times every length in one process on a synthetic prompt. The native
// configurations' run_npu2_profile_p*.lit time complete requests instead.
//
// The fused prefill reads the logical Q4 weights, so this prepares them
// (make weights-prefill, into affine-build). Latency only, never a
// correctness gate.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano, llvm_link_pre23, hfweights_allenai_olmo_2_0425_1b_instruct
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_peano_prefill_sweep
// RUN: cd test_peano_prefill_sweep
// RUN: %PYTHON %S/../bench/sweep_prefill.py --model-name olmo2_1b_q4nx --makefile %S/Makefile --lengths 512,1024,2048 --fused --make-var BUILD_DIR=../affine-build --peano-dir %PEANO_INSTALL_DIR --out olmo2_1b_q4nx.prefill_sweep.json
// RUN: FileCheck %s < olmo2_1b_q4nx.prefill_sweep.json
// CHECK: "model": "olmo2_1b_q4nx"
// CHECK: "axis": "prefill_len"
// A parsed number, not just a well-formed file: if the bench's timing line
// drifts out of sweep_prefill.py's regex every point goes null.
// CHECK: "prefill_len": 2048
// CHECK-NEXT: "ttft_ms": {{[0-9]}}
